  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The state of Virginia received $87.1B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The federal government made 307,902 awards in Virginia during the fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $283K. Obligations fell 27.7% year over year. The Department of Veterans Affairs led buying in Virginia with $31.8B in obligations, followed closely by the Department of Defense with $30.3B. Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers is the largest industry by obligation in Virginia at $28.6B, reflecting major health-related contract activity. OPTUM PUBLIC SECTOR SOLUTIONS, INC. is the top vendor with $19.9B in obligations, and TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP is the second largest vendor with $8.7B. Historical obligations show a peak of $121B in FY25 and a decline to $87.1B in FY26 to date. The data are fiscal year to date totals and represent contract obligations only, not completed spending. Contractors and agencies should note the concentration in health-related contracting and the continued prominence of the Department of Veterans Affairs and Department of Defense in Virginia procurement.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did FY2026 to date compare with prior years?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 27.7% year over year. Virginia obligated $87.1B in FY26 to date, down from $121B in FY25. The multi-year series shows growth to $121B in FY25 after $77.9B in FY21, then a decline to $87.1B in FY26 to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate federal contracting in Virginia?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $31.8B and the Department of Defense obligated $30.3B in FY2026 to date. OPTUM PUBLIC SECTOR SOLUTIONS, INC. received $19.9B and TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP received $8.7B, reflecting large vendor concentration in health-related contracts."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Virginia?",
      "a": "The state of Virginia received $87.1B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The federal government made 307,902 awards in Virginia, with an average award size of $283K. Obligations fell 27.7% year over year, and the FY series shows $77.9B in FY21, $89.4B in FY22, $106B in FY23, $110B in FY24, and $121B in FY25."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies award the most contracts in Virginia?",
      "a": "The Department of Veterans Affairs and the Department of Defense award the most contracts in Virginia. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $31.8B and the Department of Defense obligated $30.3B in FY2026 to date. Other top buyers include the Department of Homeland Security with $5.9B and the General Services Administration with $4.8B."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are the largest federal contractors in Virginia?",
      "a": "OPTUM PUBLIC SECTOR SOLUTIONS, INC. and TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP are the largest federal contractors in Virginia. OPTUM PUBLIC SECTOR SOLUTIONS, INC. received $19.9B and TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP received $8.7B in FY2026 to date. LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION, ATLANTIC DIVING SUPPLY, INC., and HUNTINGTON INGALLS INC follow with $3B, $2.9B, and $2.8B respectively."
